   $q$Which sentence would best fill the blank in sentence 6 by explaining what the evidence in sentence 5 shows?$q$, $q$[{"text":"These results prove that still stretches cause almost every soccer injury that players suffer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"},{"text":"These results suggest that moving warm-ups helped players both perform better and stay healthier during the season.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The season lasted several months, and the players practiced four times every week.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"new-detail-without-analysis"},{"text":"High knees are an exercise in which players lift each knee toward the chest while jogging.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"definition-not-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$These results suggest that moving warm-ups helped players both perform better and stay healthier during the season.$q$, $q$Sentence 5 gives two results, faster sprints and fewer missed practices, and the correct choice explains what both mean. The choice about still stretches causing almost every injury goes far beyond what the study measured.$q$, 'draft', 'bd5f01da-1909-5142-a91a-1d328e26d8ef')
