-- Passage wg9-writing-with-evidence-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('11a69fea-2e57-5b33-a9bd-ba786f7c0aed', 'wg9-writing-with-evidence-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Reading While Watching$q$, $q$(1) In the article "Words on the Screen," education researcher Samuel Adeyemi reports on a study of students learning a new language through short videos. (2) Videos are a common part of many classes today. (3) Adeyemi's team showed the same ten Spanish cartoons to 120 ninth graders, but only half of the students saw Spanish captions at the bottom of the screen. (4) After each video, every student took a short quiz on new vocabulary words. (5) The students who watched with captions scored an average of 18 percent higher on the quizzes. (6) ____, they remembered more of the words when they were tested again a month later.

(7) Adeyemi suggests a reason for these results. (8) Adeyemi explains that captions let students see and hear a word at the same time, which gives the brain two ways to remember it. (9) Some students in the study said the captions also helped them follow fast speakers. (10) My cousin always watches movies with the captions turned on. (11) This shows that captions are not a distraction but a tool that helps learners connect sounds with written words.

(12) ____$q$, 'draft')
