-- Passage wg9-writing-with-evidence-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1e122d82-b647-57bc-8510-ed2ddb338831', 'wg9-writing-with-evidence-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Pencils in the Gallery$q$, $q$(1) In "Look Longer," museum educator Rafael Tanaka writes about a change at the Harborview Art Museum, which began handing out free sketchbooks and pencils at its entrance. (2) Tanaka argues that sketching helps visitors notice far more than they would by simply walking past the art. (3) Tanaka explains that museum staff timed visitors in front of a large painting of a harbor at sunset. (4) Visitors without sketchbooks looked at the painting for an average of nineteen seconds. (5) Visitors who sketched it stayed for an average of eleven minutes. (6) ____

(7) Tanaka also describes what the sketchers noticed. (8) In short interviews after their visits, sketchers mentioned details such as a small dog on the dock and the way the light changed color across the water. (9) Most visitors who did not sketch could describe only the sunset itself. (10) The museum's gift shop sells postcards of the painting for two dollars each. (11) ____, the act of drawing seems to turn a quick glance into careful study.

(12) In conclusion, I think museums are fun places to visit on weekends.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
