   $q$Which sentence would best fill the blank in sentence 6 by explaining what the evidence in sentences 4 and 5 shows?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Eleven minutes is equal to six hundred sixty seconds, which is a long time to stand still.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"math-not-analysis"},{"text":"This proves that people who cannot draw well should not visit art museums at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The painting of the harbor hangs in the largest room on the museum's second floor.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"new-detail-without-analysis"},{"text":"This large difference suggests that sketching slows visitors down and leads them to study the painting closely.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$This large difference suggests that sketching slows visitors down and leads them to study the painting closely.$q$, $q$The correct choice explains what the jump from nineteen seconds to eleven minutes means for the claim about noticing more. Converting minutes to seconds is accurate, but it only restates the number without explaining its importance.$q$, 'draft', '1e122d82-b647-57bc-8510-ed2ddb338831')
