  ('9270011c-71ea-533f-9505-0091c51a542d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which revision of sentence 12 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Painting a sunset is difficult because the colors in the sky change so quickly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"Every museum in the world should require all visitors to sketch every painting they see.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Tanaka's evidence shows that sketching keeps visitors looking much longer and helps them notice details others miss.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Tanaka writes about the Harborview Art Museum and its free sketchbooks and pencils.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Tanaka's evidence shows that sketching keeps visitors looking much longer and helps them notice details others miss.$q$, $q$The conclusion should restate the claim using both kinds of evidence, the longer viewing time and the details noticed. Requiring every visitor to sketch every painting is far beyond what Tanaka's study supports.$q$, 'draft', '1e122d82-b647-57bc-8510-ed2ddb338831')
