-- Passage wg9-writing-with-evidence-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('602f6ab6-9b85-57fe-8cfa-73635c90d39c', 'wg9-writing-with-evidence-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: The Share Table$q$, $q$(1) Environmental reporter Leila Haddad's article "Saved from the Trash" examines a share table in the cafeteria at Westbrook High School. (2) Haddad's evidence suggests that a simple table can cut food waste and help students who are still hungry. (3) A share table is a spot where students leave unopened food they do not want, such as a sealed yogurt or a whole apple, so that others can take it. (4) ____ (5) Haddad adds that the custodial staff now empties one fewer trash bin after each lunch period, since far fewer sealed snacks and pieces of fruit end up thrown away.

(6) The table also helps students directly. (7) Haddad interviewed a cafeteria worker who noticed that athletes with late practices often pick up extra fruit before leaving. (8) Some students who skip breakfast also stop by the table for a second item at lunch. (9) Students like the share table a lot. (10) Apples are one of the most common fruits grown in the country. (11) Haddad does point out one challenge: staff must check the table each day to make sure nothing spoils.

(12) ____$q$, 'draft')
